    35	## What provable intention means
    36	
    37	Developers specify contract invariants and transition rules. Users authorize canonical, machine-readable outcome and authority constraints. Candidate execution must satisfy both. Natural-language wishes require explicit formalization and an inspectable signing display; a proof cannot establish that a misunderstood specification matches an unexpressed wish.
